WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.780
Sudden heat shocks alter honey bee gut microbiomes and raise mortality more than sustained heat waves. This is Planetarian Daily, Episode 248. After the bees assigns deep dive on owner habits and dogs, a machine that builds long protein chains, and eagles taking adult baboons. Washington State University researchers, in a Fizz.org report on work published in scientific reports, exposed newly emerged honey bees from six colonies to three temperature regimes in enclosures.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:34.320
Bees held under continuous elevated temperature adapted with lower damage than the shock groups.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:40.140
The team tested both optimal and supplemented diets across groups of 150 bees each.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.400
Hormesis appears to explain why rapid temperature change produce greater effects than steady

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:45.780
stress.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.860
Something most people get wrong is the idea that a dog's gut microbes are an isolated

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.880
pet health matter that stops at the bull.

00:00:53.796 --> 00:00:58.696
A study of hundreds of dogs across four nations found that pet owners daily habits influence

00:00:58.696 --> 00:01:04.536
the microbial communities inside their dogs. Yesterday, it was waste water bacteria from eight Ohio

00:01:04.536 --> 00:01:11.336
cities, serving 1.3 million people, with associations to local rates of obesity, high blood pressure,

00:01:11.616 --> 00:01:17.096
asthma, and depression. Today's canine work adds that owner routines shape the microbes living in

00:01:17.096 --> 00:01:22.436
animals that share those surroundings. The research underscores how shared environments link human

00:01:22.436 --> 00:01:27.676
and canine health rather than treating those ecosystems as separate. Everyday surroundings and

00:01:27.676 --> 00:01:32.916
rapid change both quietly reshape biology across species, from a kennel to a hive.

00:01:33.808 --> 00:01:40.848
An MIT machine, according to PSU Connect, assembled a 164 amino acid protein chain through

00:01:40.848 --> 00:01:43.608
327 sequential reactions and hours.

00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:48.848
Researchers can now order exact sequences from suppliers and receive them within weeks,

00:01:49.128 --> 00:01:53.288
which lets labs run side-by-side tests of single amino acid variants.

00:01:53.288 --> 00:01:59.828
Staple peptides use hydrocarbon bridges to lock alpha helices that otherwise unwind, raising

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:06.868
helical content in 1 MDM2 and MDMX binding sequence from 11% to 70%.

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:13.568
Beta amino acid substitutions in glucagon-like peptide 1 or GLP1 analogs shifted receptor

00:02:13.568 --> 00:02:18.368
signaling balance between G protein and beta arrestin pathways and cultured cells.

00:02:18.368 --> 00:02:24.188
The Rata-16i peptide forms a fully defined gel that supports three-dimensional cell growth,

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:29.428
and alters chemotherapy response in ovarian cancer spheroids compared with flat cultures.

00:02:30.465 --> 00:02:35.085
Talon punctures on skulls and characteristic shoulder bone marks turned up on adult male

00:02:35.085 --> 00:02:40.525
baboons in Chad's NETI Plateau, documented by University of St. Andrews researchers

00:02:40.525 --> 00:02:42.125
in a Fizz.org report.

00:02:42.785 --> 00:02:47.745
One individual weighed over 26 kilograms, within the range of some hominin species.

00:02:47.745 --> 00:02:53.005
The finding challenges the assumption that primates above 13 kilograms escaped aerial

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.545
predation for the past two and a half million years.

00:02:56.185 --> 00:03:00.965
Baboons responded with alarm calls and dropped to safety specifically when Verose eagles

00:03:00.965 --> 00:03:01.785
flew overhead.

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:07.705
A United Nations Environment Program and World Health Organization report estimates annual

00:03:07.705 --> 00:03:13.345
health and environmental cost from endocrine disrupting chemical, or EDC exposure exceed

00:03:13.345 --> 00:03:14.645
one trillion dollars.

00:03:14.645 --> 00:03:20.685
The assessment reviewed thousands of studies on bisfinals, thalates, and parabens, and found

00:03:20.685 --> 00:03:25.985
the strongest links to neurological conditions and reproductive problems, including sperm decline.

00:03:26.765 --> 00:03:31.185
Evidence also connects EDCs to rising rates of type 2 diabetes and asthma.

00:03:31.985 --> 00:03:36.985
Workers and chemicals and recycling industries face the highest exposure, with one-two-thousand

00:03:36.985 --> 00:03:42.305
24-risk band study detecting over 20 hazardous chemicals in Thai and Kenyan participants.

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:47.385
Roughly 1,000 EDCs have been identified, though many remain untested.

00:03:48.363 --> 00:03:52.603
Researchers built a composite climate pressure index from greenhouse gas emissions,

00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:58.663
particulate exposure, temperature volatility, and precipitation volatility, with the analysis

00:03:58.663 --> 00:04:00.503
appearing in sustainable development.

00:04:00.943 --> 00:04:07.663
The work covered 23 emerging market economies from 2002 to 2022, and linked higher climate

00:04:07.663 --> 00:04:13.763
pressure to increased inequality across Gini coefficient, Paul Maratio and Thile index measures.

00:04:14.203 --> 00:04:18.423
Per capita income and institutional quality correlated with lower inequality,

00:04:18.903 --> 00:04:24.478
while unemployment correlated with higher inequality. High harmonic generation produces new

00:04:24.478 --> 00:04:29.758
frequencies many times higher than the driving laser beam. Paul's to pulse fluctuations in the

00:04:29.758 --> 00:04:35.358
emitted light carry additional information beyond brightness and spectrum about how electrons move

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:42.712
in solids. A strategic management journal analysis of U.S. job postings from 2010 to 2022

00:04:43.122 --> 00:04:47.952
found firms increasing AIU's posted more managerial vacancies rather than fewer.

00:04:48.552 --> 00:04:54.151
The study linked AI adoption to shifts in required managerial skills. University of

00:04:54.151 --> 00:04:59.351
Cordoba researchers surveyed Sierra Nevada and Sierra Delos-Philabris and found invasive

00:04:59.351 --> 00:05:05.051
plants concentrated near road edges, declining sharply at higher elevations. The work highlights

00:05:05.051 --> 00:05:10.319
vulnerability of these ecosystems to future climate-driven spread. Gender differences

00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:15.199
in values across Europe showed no overall widening, despite media focus on young men's

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:19.759
conservatism. The pattern appears driven by social and conventional media coverage,

00:05:19.959 --> 00:05:25.515
rather than population-level trends. Researchers at ICFO developed a microscope that

00:05:25.515 --> 00:05:31.475
resolves single atoms in strontium quantum gases in one shot. Earlier work imaged Bosonic

00:05:31.475 --> 00:05:36.415
extruntium 84, the new system extends capability to additional atomic species.

00:05:37.432 --> 00:05:42.672
Famue FSU College of Engineering Scientists created a gel that releases therapeutic particles

00:05:42.672 --> 00:05:44.432
at sites of spinal cord injury.

00:05:45.072 --> 00:05:49.052
The material aims to support recovery of damaged cells in laboratory models.

00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:54.966
In brief, a new planning tool ranks Chilean restoration sites by extinction risk reduction,

00:05:55.506 --> 00:06:01.806
carbon storage, riparian restoration, and feasibility, and shows that 80.4% of priority areas

00:06:01.806 --> 00:06:03.266
has served more than one objective.

00:06:03.946 --> 00:06:06.646
University of Canterbury researcher Peter Pelser

00:06:06.646 --> 00:06:08.346
received taxonomic recognition

00:06:08.346 --> 00:06:10.986
with the South American daisy genus Pelseria.

00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:14.066
A new Asian flying frog species from Indonesia

00:06:14.066 --> 00:06:16.386
shows distinctive morphology, calls,

00:06:16.846 --> 00:06:19.086
and egg-laying behavior in mountain rain forests.

00:06:19.906 --> 00:06:22.306
Lasers approaching physical miniaturization limits

00:06:22.306 --> 00:06:25.586
now enable nanoscale tracking of biological processes,

00:06:26.126 --> 00:06:28.946
including organelle and molecular complex dynamics.

00:06:28.946 --> 00:06:34.986
Insect feed made from food waste carries a low bovine spongeiform and cephalopathy, or

00:06:34.986 --> 00:06:40.286
BSE transmission risk, with analysis indicating permitted waste streams pose minimal prior

00:06:40.286 --> 00:06:41.866
on risk under current controls.

00:06:42.586 --> 00:06:49.166
Isotope tracing in sea elegans posted on BioRXIV showed declining incorporation of nicotinamide

00:06:49.166 --> 00:06:56.246
and nicotinic acid into nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide, or NAD, despite rising co-factor abundance.

00:06:56.246 --> 00:07:02.906
The SCP-Viz single-cell proteomics toolkit processes data from any common workflow and showed

00:07:02.906 --> 00:07:07.686
comparable protein depth and drug response patterns in stored versus fresh cancer cell

00:07:07.686 --> 00:07:08.246
digests.

00:07:08.786 --> 00:07:17.386
An analysis of 2,559 families and 6,710 twin pairs found a 0.68 correlation between

00:07:17.386 --> 00:07:22.926
genetic nurture estimates and classical shared environment variants, strongest for educational

00:07:22.926 --> 00:07:23.606
outcomes.

00:07:23.606 --> 00:07:30.126
Before we go, many of those roughly 1000 identified endocrine disrupting chemicals remain untested.

